# Final solution recipe (base-only log+prob stack)

Reproduce with `workspaces/bellatrix_tau/make_final_candidate.py` (writes `meta_candidate_submission.csv`).

1. Collect every `workspaces/*/oof_<name>.npy` + matching `test_<name>.npy`.
2. Exclude derived/partial files by **substring**: `stack, blend, optblend, mystack, crossstack, partial, chosen, sub, candidate, nested, meta_`. Never include `*partial*`.
3. Normalize rows to sum 1; drop any base model with OOF logloss > 0.75.
4. Deduplicate near-identical models: sort by OOF logloss, keep a model only if corr(flatten(OOF)) <= 0.998 with every kept model.
5. Meta-features per row: concatenation of `log(p_k)` and raw `p_k` for all kept base models (columns EAP,HPL,MWS).
6. Multinomial LogisticRegression, C=0.1, max_iter=4000; 5-fold CV with shared `StratifiedKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)` folds (`fold_id.npy`) gives OOF logloss **0.20416** at time of writing.
7. Fit on all OOF rows, predict test, write `id,EAP,HPL,MWS` (rows sum to 1).

Base pool includes TF-IDF/NB/SVM/GBM models from all agents plus transformer OOFs (`dbl5`, `dbl5_s2`, `deberta_base_ls`, `roberta_large_snap`, ...). Level-1 stack features were tested and rejected by leak-free nested CV. No post-processing/temperature needed (T=1 optimal on OOF).

References: `bellatrix_tau_stacking_insight.md`, `bellatrix_tau_transformer_breaks_stack.md`, `bellatrix_tau_stack_logprob_plus_prob.md`, `canopus_kappa_submission_s1.md`, `mirfak_pi_0206.md`.
